TI  - Prediction of sulfide formation in sewer pressure mains based on the IWA Anaerobic Digestion Model No. 1 (ADM1).
AU  - Freudenthal, K
AU  - Koglatis, J
AU  - Otterpohl, R
AU  - Behrendt, J
JO  - Water science and technology : a journal of the International Association on Water Pollution Research
PY  - 2005
AB  - In this paper a new approach is presented to predict sulfide formation in sewers based on the IWA Anaerobic Digestion Model No. 1 (ADM1). Compared with existing models the ADM1 has two crucial advantages. Firstly, it simulates anaerobic digestion processes, of which sulfide formation is the final step. Secondly, it uses a more detailed description of the waste water composition. In order to obtain reliable data for calculation an experimental set-up for measuring the Oxygen Uptake Rate (OUR) is used. An implementation of sulfide formation processes into the model matrix is proposed.
